* LEQ_model.lib -- three interchangeable implementations of the same
* LEQ_MODEL subckt (same name + pin interface in every section):
*   ideal  : single ideal inductor, L=1.3723n
*   rl     : EM-derived series L+R, L=1.3723n R=1.6674ohm
*   snp2le : snp2le broadband vector-fitted macromodel (same EM data)
* Select the active one from the including file via:
*   .lib <path>/LEQ_model.lib ideal   (or rl, or snp2le)

.lib ideal
.SUBCKT LEQ_MODEL p1
L1 p1 0 1.3723n
.ENDS LEQ_MODEL
.endl ideal

.lib rl
.SUBCKT LEQ_MODEL p1
L1 p1 mid_LEQ 1.3723n
R1 mid_LEQ 0 1.6674
.ENDS LEQ_MODEL
.endl rl

.lib snp2le
* LEQ_MODEL - lumped-element equivalent (Ngspice / SPICE3)
* generated by snp2le 0.1.18
* EQUIVALENT CIRCUIT FOR VECTOR FITTED S-MATRIX
* Created using scikit-rf vectorFitting.py
* 
* 
* thermal noise of the passive: kT(I - S S^H) at the ports, from a spectral factor of this fit
* sources Rnz_e1..Rnz_e1 (0.25 ohm, the only noisy elements), 6 states nz_x*, controlled sources Gnz_*
* DC pin: Y = Y_fit + dY / (1 + s/wc), fc = 160 Hz, so the model meets the file's 0 Hz point. Nodes dcp_d*, controlled sources Gdcp_*, noiseless
